strong class='sig'>+0.65\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.25 to +1.05). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months; 4 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Clarksburg's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.29 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 44.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 1996 (63.87 in); the driest, 1930 (21.65 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}